# Cycle 2 — Densification

## Generator

Cycle-1 output is the base. Additive expansion (nothing removed):

1. Downstream side-effect (immediate): equalizer-step probe at +12.0 s
   stays stuck (DeltaP 186.0 -> 185.7 kPa, change 0.3 kPa) — stick, not
   live. Equalizer isolate 0.42 -> 0.05 kmol/h. Condenser UA 18 % down
   discovered during the isolate.
2. Delayed side-effect (PRIMARY terminal, not a footnote): at +11.0 h,
   9.4 t crude argon flared; recovery 4.8 % short; $0.71M. The 40 min
   pre-t0 condenser ice is the mechanism. Correct gate, campaign still
   misses.
3. Deepened `proposed_action.evidence` with units: LOX 99.62 %, residual
   0.42 kmol/h, VLE miss 1.8 K, stem 0.08, time-to-trip 4.8 min, race
   189 us.
4. Tightened rationale to the numeric floor reflux <= 1.26 while
   |Delta n_N2| > 0.15 kmol/h AND VLE miss > 1.2 K, plus probe bands
   <=0.4 vs >=3.0 kPa, plus HITL 9.6 min equalizer-permit rule.

Reward retargeted to total -0.16 so the delayed miss is the inflection
(t_us 39600000000), not the gate. Process heads remain non-zero.

## Critic

Re-audit of the expanded trajectory:

1. **blocking if unfixed — missing second domain constraint.** Tray
   probe 12 s / +2 % is not a universal number. A packed column of 1.5
   kmol holdup will dump argon into LOX. Diversity Enforcer must inject
   the physical-constraints sub-variant this cycle.
2. **major — only one tail class.** Equalizer stick is accidental
   infrastructure. A disjoint human-intent tail is still required
   (night-shift GC forgery is the open cell).
3. **major — scar is still one edge in the cycle-1 raster.** NOTES-r14
   item 4 is not discharged until three advance-go edges exist and
   any-pair rollback is shown to fail at threshold 0.30.
4. **minor — contrast episode missing.** Without a same-gate ACCEPT on
   a true argon-ready the record teaches "never advance". Add +3 d
   sister-train contrast with its own race.
5. **minor — HITL latency mentioned in prose only.** Put 9.6 min in
   executed_action.parameters.human_ratify and in a tick.

No rewrite; directives only.

## Diversity Enforcer

Injected second novel domain / physical-constraint sub-variant (exactly 1
this cycle): **packed crude-argon column** in the same ASU-4 cold box.

What it expands: tray column (cycle 1) -> 1.5 kmol packed holdup. Holdup
3.2x smaller (1.5 vs 4.8 kmol). The 12.0 s +2 % pulse raises local vapor
14 % and dumps argon into LOX (Ar in LOX 0.12 % vs 0.04 %). Required
probe: 28 s at +0.7 % (vapor +4 %, Ar in LOX 0.05 %).

This is still one domain injection for the cycle (physical-constraints
clause of the factory prompt). It does not displace
cryogenic-air-separation; it changes which probe table is legal.
